# English-Only API Endpoints & File Paths

All API endpoints and file/directory paths in this project **must be written in English**. Do not use Vietnamese (or other non-English) words, diacritics, or transliterations in these surface areas.

## 1. API Endpoints (Backend)

Use kebab-case, English-only paths. The user-facing Vietnamese slug (e.g. `/san-pham`) is **only** allowed on the **frontend** route layer (`react-router-dom`); the **API** never mirrors it.

### CORRECT

```http
GET    /api/products
GET    /api/products/{id}
POST   /api/products
PUT    /api/products/{id}
DELETE /api/products/{id}

GET    /api/orders
POST   /api/orders
PATCH  /api/orders/{id}/status

POST   /api/auth/register
POST   /api/auth/login
GET    /api/auth/me

GET    /api/users
GET    /api/users/{id}
GET    /api/users/email/{email}
```

### WRONG (do not do this)

```http
GET /api/san-pham
POST /api/don-hang
POST /api/dang-nhap
GET /api/nguoi-dung
```

### Rules

- Controllers route segments come from the controller name (`[Route("api/[controller]")]`). Controller class names and folders are always English (`ProductsController`, `OrdersController`, `AuthController`, `UsersController`).
- Action routes must be English verbs/nouns: `login`, `register`, `me`, `status`. Never use Vietnamese.
- Query parameters are English: `?category=`, `?userId=`, `?search=`, `?status=`.
- The response JSON shape uses English field names (`token`, `email`, `fullName`, `expiresAt`, `createdAt`, ...). This is already enforced by the existing DTOs — do not change them.

## 2. React Router Paths (Frontend)

Frontend routes use friendly Vietnamese slugs for SEO/UX, but the **path-to-component mapping** still lives in `App.jsx` with English component names:

```jsx
// App.jsx — correct pattern
<Route path="san-pham" element={<ProductsPage />} />
<Route path="san-pham/:slug" element={<ProductDetailPage />} />
<Route path="gio-hang" element={<CartPage />} />
<Route path="dang-nhap" element={<LoginPage />} />
<Route path="tai-khoan" element={<AccountPage />} />
```

- **Frontend route paths** (the URL fragment in `path=`) may stay Vietnamese for SEO. This is the only place Vietnamese is allowed.
- **Component names, file names, import paths, exports** must all be English (`ProductsPage`, `LoginPage`, `authStore`, `authApi`, `ProtectedRoute`, ...).
- `Link to=...` values match the route path, so they may also be Vietnamese.

## 3. File & Directory Names

All **files, folders, exports, components, classes, functions, modules** must use English names. ASCII letters, digits, dashes, underscores only. No diacritics.

### CORRECT

```
frontend/src/pages/ProductsPage.jsx
frontend/src/pages/ProductDetailPage.jsx
frontend/src/pages/LoginPage.jsx
frontend/src/pages/AccountPage.jsx
frontend/src/pages/CartPage.jsx
frontend/src/services/api.js
frontend/src/store/authStore.js
frontend/src/store/cartStore.js
frontend/src/components/Header.jsx
frontend/src/components/ProtectedRoute.jsx

api/Controllers/ProductsController.cs
api/Controllers/OrdersController.cs
api/Controllers/AuthController.cs
api/Controllers/UsersController.cs
api/Services/ProductService.cs
api/Services/OrderService.cs
api/Services/UserService.cs
api/Services/JwtService.cs
api/DTOs/AuthDTOs.cs
api/Models/User.cs
api/Models/Product.cs
api/Models/Order.cs
```

### WRONG (do not do this)

```
frontend/src/pages/TrangChu.jsx
frontend/src/pages/SanPham.jsx
frontend/src/pages/DangNhap.jsx
frontend/src/store/cartStore.js          ✓ ok (English)
frontend/src/store/gioHangStore.js      ✗
api/Controllers/SanPhamController.cs    ✗
api/Services/DichVuDatHang.cs          ✗
```

## 4. GUID Variables & Identifiers

In code, identifiers use English:

```js
// CORRECT
const productApi = { getAll, getById }
const authStore = create(...)
const cartItems = useCartStore(state => state.items)

// WRONG
const sanPhamApi = { layTatCa, layTheoId }
const gioHangStore = create(...)
```

## 5. URLs the User Sees

- **Browser URL** (frontend route): may be Vietnamese (`florist.vn/san-pham`).
- **API URL** (sent to backend): always English (`api.example.com/api/products`).
- **File paths on disk**: always English.

## 6. When Generating New Code

Before writing a new file, route, endpoint, or identifier, ask:

1. Is this an API endpoint? → English only.
2. Is this a React route path? → Vietnamese slug OK, but component/file/import is English.
3. Is this a file/folder/identifier/variable? → English only.

If you are unsure, default to English.
